 "text": "Hi, how can I help you? Well, the best way to start a campfire is by using a small, dry, and flat piece of wood. You can use a twig to get the fire started, but make sure it's not too big or too wet. Yes, cotton balls. Yes, they can be used to start a fire, especially if you're in a survival situation. Of course, I packed them for the trip. The fire should be small enough to keep you warm, but not too big to burn your hand. For tea, you can use twigs or small branches to get the fire started. To put out the fire, you can use dirt or other dry materials to extinguish the flames.",
